# Normalize every tracked text file to LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree of a fresh clone, on any platform. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true`
# (the Windows default in many setups) materialises source files as CRLF, and
# any test or tool that compares tracked source text against a bare-newline
# literal fails on a clean checkout while passing locally.
#
# This exact defect class already cost pi-telegram-bridge one GitHub Actions
# run: see its `test(ci)` commits. Cheap to prevent, expensive to debug.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells are the exception: cmd.exe and Windows PowerShell are the
# environments where CRLF is still the safe expectation.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
